{
  "category": "Electric Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It rotates its arms to generate electricity, but it tires easily, so it charges up only a little bit.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even in the most vicious storm, this POKéMON plays happily if thunder rumbles in the sky.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It loves violent thunder. The space between its horns flickers bluish- white when it is charging energy.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "ELEKID stores electricity in its body. If it touches metal and accidentally discharges all its built-up electricity, this POKéMON begins swinging its arms in circles to recharge itself.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "ELEKID stores electricity in its body. If it touches metal and accidentally discharges all its built-up electricity, this POKéMON begins swinging its arms in circles to recharge itself.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "If it touches metal and discharges the electricity it has stored in its body, an ELEKID begins swinging its arms in circles to recharge itself.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even in the most vicious storm, this POKéMON plays happily if thunder rumbles in the sky.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rotates its arms to generate electricity, but it tires easily, so it charges up only a little bit.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It generates electricity by whirling its arms. However, it can’t store the energy it makes.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It generates electricity by whirling its arms. However, it can’t store the energy it makes.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "A weak electric current flows between its horns. Sticking a hand there shocks the unwary.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It rotates its arms to generate electricity, but it tires easily, so it only charges up a little bit.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Even in the most vicious storm, this Pokémon plays happily if thunder rumbles in the sky.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "A weak electric current flows between its horns. Sticking a hand there shocks the unwary.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "A weak electric current flows between its horns. Sticking a hand there shocks the unwary.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spinning its arms around to generate electricity makes the area between its horns shine light blue.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spinning its arms around to generate electricity makes the area between its horns shine light blue.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It generates electricity by whirling its arms. However, it can’t store the energy it makes.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Spinning its arms around to generate electricity makes the area between its horns shine light blue.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elekid stores electricity in its body. If it touches metal and accidentally discharges all its built-up electricity, this Pokémon begins swinging its arms in circles to recharge itself.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elekid stores electricity in its body. If it touches metal and accidentally discharges all its built-up electricity, this Pokémon begins swinging its arms in circles to recharge itself.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it’s in a house, electrical outlets serve as its baby bottles. It sucks down electricity.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is constantly fighting with Togedemaru that try to steal its electricity. It’s a pretty even match.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it hears the crash of thunder, Elekid’s mood improves. It can be useful to record that sound and play it when Elekid’s feeling down.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its horns shine a bluish white, that’s the sign it’s fully charged. You’ll get a shocking jolt if you touch it!",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "When a storm approaches, this Pokémon gets restless. Once Elekid hears the sound of thunder, it gets full-on rowdy.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s not good at storing electricity yet. This Pokémon sneaks into people’s homes, looking for electrical outlets to eat electricity from.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "They generate electricity by spinning their arms. During a thunderstorm, if one hears the lively voices of children out in the wilderness, what one is actually hearing are the voices of Elekid.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
